From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: premohq <48417750+premohq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:05:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: Ocarina of Time's mesh draws
 skipped again, as they stopped the GPU

On PS5-680 Ocarina of Time stopped the GPU at the first task/mesh draw of gameplay, three runs in a
row (VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST 10 s later, at 54-77 s), with its helper calls lowered and with
EglantinePS5's own GPU shortcuts. Core patch 0075 (WIP in EglantinePS5) issues the mesh-only draws
that 0071 skipped. With EDEN_OOT_MESH_DRAWS=skip in env.txt the game went past that point and
played on. It is now one of the core switches' defaults, which env.txt still overrides
(EDEN_OOT_MESH_DRAWS=draw for work on them). Trees' leaves are missing, as with 0071.
---
 headless/main.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/headless/main.cpp b/headless/main.cpp
index 5502859..af79f87 100644
--- a/headless/main.cpp
+++ b/headless/main.cpp
@@ -669,10 +669,14 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv) {
         // pages with nothing to flush answer on the guest core instead of waiting for the GPU
         // thread, as they do with fastmem (Mario Kart World's title screen: 13 -> 20 FPS). The
         // three waits poll 300 us before sleeping: a wake-up here is a system call on both sides.
+        // Playtendoh: Ocarina of Time's task and mesh draws are all skipped, as core patch 0071 had
+        // them. 0075 issues the mesh-only ones, and on PS5-680 the GPU stopped at the first of them
+        // every time (VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST 10 s later); with them skipped the game plays on.
         for (const auto& [name, value] : {std::pair{"EDEN_NX2_UNSAFE_PREEMPTIVE_READS", "1"},
                                           std::pair{"EDEN_PS5_READ_SPIN_US", "300"},
                                           std::pair{"EDEN_PS5_GPU_SPIN_US", "300"},
-                                          std::pair{"EDEN_PS5_WORKER_SPIN_US", "300"}}) {
+                                          std::pair{"EDEN_PS5_WORKER_SPIN_US", "300"},
+                                          std::pair{"EDEN_OOT_MESH_DRAWS", "skip"}}) {
             setenv(name, value, 0);
         }
         // The 64-bit fastmem window (src/host_memory.cpp, Window64): opt-in while it is qualified,
